AltoStaking::getContainerAfterProcessing()
├── given container does not exist
│   └── it should return empty container data with default values
├── given container exists but is not active
│   └── it should return container data with multiplier and deprecated status
├── given container exists and is active
│   ├── when epoch has no TVL data
│   │   └── it should return container with minimum duration as next duration
│   ├── when epoch has TVL data
│   │   └── it should return container with calculated next duration based on TVL share
│   └── when container is deprecated
│       └── it should return container with isDeprecated set to true
└── given epoch to process is valid
    └── it should return extended container with all fields including currentDurationEpochsNext
